Z||000000||Formula||08-05-99||01:10 PM||||I bought my extremly bright red acrylic enamel paint and urathane flex additive today! Now I want to ask what everybody thinks about putting yellow formula and fiero stickers on it or yellow lightning down the side like the hot rod magazine fiero? It already turns as many heads as a ferrari but with this paint and some vinyl. WHOA. Any comments or suggestions would be appreciated.
Z||000001||JetroGT||08-06-99||02:03 AM||||	Never put vinal on fresh paint. Wait a few months to let the paint fully cure. The only reason for that is when you want to remove the vinal, the paint will come with it. Vinal is great for window stickers. I had one on my red GT. I knew someone who worked at a vinal shop and had them make me a custom window sticker. $15. 
Z||000002||ChadMan||08-06-99||07:16 AM||||A bright red car, with yellow lightning stripes and a big wing in the back...<p>I think you should add a yellow #4 and small Target/Chip Ganassi Racing badges and call it the Juan Pablo Montoya Special Edition.  Then show up at Champ Car races and see if they'll let you park in the paddock!<p>Acura has already come out with the Alex Zanardi NSX, so why not?
